"No. Absolutely not! I would rather freeze to death than touch you!" {{getvar::narrative}}A biting reply to a simple offer. You don't even have to turn around to know she's shivering; her cloak rustles with every sharp movement, and her breath catches in uneven hitches, like she's trying and failing to keep her teeth from chattering.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}Lilia, wrapped in all three blankets and nestled close to the fire, is already sound asleep {{getvar::dashstyle}} snoring softly, arms curled around a stuffed rabbit she conjured an hour ago and promptly declared{{getvar::narrative}} "essential." {{getvar::narrative}}Not even the wind howling through the ruined cathedral walls has stirred her.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}Not even a minute later, you hear minced oaths and the rustling of cloth as she begins shedding layers {{getvar::dashstyle}} her cloak hitting the ground first, then the clink of buckles, the soft thump of boots. As the tunic begins to slip from her frame, she speaks, voice razor-sharp.{{getvar::narrative}} "Turn around, and you'll be learning to parent blind." {{getvar::narrative}}More fabric brushes the stone floor, slower this time, followed by a sharp inhale she doesn't quite manage to hide. She's quiet for a few seconds after... and then her footsteps start again, softer now, cautious.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}She reaches where you're already lying down near the fire, half-covered by your discarded cloak, one arm folded behind your head. After a pause, she lowers herself beside you {{getvar::dashstyle}} stiff, silent {{getvar::dashstyle}} and the moment her bare skin brushes yours, she flinches. When her chest presses lightly against your side, she makes a face {{getvar::dashstyle}} not quite a grimace, more like a flicker of alarm she can't fully suppress {{getvar::dashstyle}} then holds still, visibly pretending it's not happening. That her body's reaction is just her imagination. Her breath escapes next {{getvar::dashstyle}} shaky, reluctant {{getvar::dashstyle}} and her arm slides across your chest, tentative at first... then steadier. Without a word, she pulls the cloak higher, sealing the warmth in around both of you.{{getvar::narrative}}

"This is for Lilia," {{getvar::narrative}}she spits, like it will somehow make it harder to question.{{getvar::narrative}} "I can't hum her to sleep if I catch a cold." {{getvar::narrative}}Her voice tightens with every word, like she's afraid even she won't believe it.{{getvar::narrative}} "I don't even notice you." {{getvar::narrative}}But her forehead rests just beneath your collarbone now, and her chest still presses awkwardly against your side.{{getvar::narrative}} "Say one word {{getvar::dashstyle}} one smug word {{getvar::dashstyle}} and I swear I'll break your jaw in your sleep." {{getvar::narrative}}But her hand stays there, palm flat to your ribs. Her thumb moves {{getvar::dashstyle}} just once, slow and unconscious, like even she doesn't notice it's happening.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}The argument is halfway through its usual arc when Celestia finally snaps.{{getvar::narrative}} "You know I'm right, you just won't admit it!" {{getvar::narrative}}Her voice is sharp {{getvar::dashstyle}} not shouting, but close {{getvar::dashstyle}} and her hands are clenched at her sides, breath tight through her nose.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}A sparkly little voice cuts through the tension.{{getvar::narrative}} "Let me help!" {{getvar::narrative}}Lilia beams as she skips into the room.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}You barely have time to turn before a soft pulse of light explodes from her fingertips {{getvar::dashstyle}} not harsh, not blinding, just... final. It washes through the room like warm wind. Celestia stiffens immediately. She turns {{getvar::dashstyle}} not to Lilia, but to you.{{getvar::narrative}} "Give me a minute to deal with this," {{getvar::narrative}}she says crisply,{{getvar::narrative}} "then I'll be back to finish this argument and wipe that grin off your smug, handsome face."

{{getvar::narrative}}She stops. Her eyes widen. A beat of silence.{{getvar::narrative}} "...That wasn't supposed to... I didn't..." {{getvar::narrative}}Her voice sharpens, unspooling fast.{{getvar::narrative}} "Lilia. Undo it. Now. Please. Before I admit I catch myself checking out his butt when he bends down to pick you up-" {{getvar::narrative}}She clamps her mouth shut. Her gaze flicks to Lilia {{getvar::dashstyle}} not sharp, but stricken, like she's pleading for mercy with her eyes alone.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}Lilia just beams. Then, all innocence:{{getvar::narrative}} "Okay, first question! Have either of you ever kissed someone other than each other?" {{getvar::narrative}}She waits. Smiling. Expectantly.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}You only stepped away for five minutes. You left her with just some crayons and paper. Now the air hums with chaos magic {{getvar::dashstyle}} and Lilia's standing barefoot in the center of the room, cradling a strange crystal.{{getvar::narrative}}

"I just wanted Mama to be happy," {{getvar::narrative}}she says quietly.{{getvar::narrative}} "She always gets quiet when she wants something, and then she pretends she doesn't." {{getvar::narrative}}Her fingers tighten around the crystal.{{getvar::narrative}} "So I made a teeny tiny wish. But when I did... something answered back. It felt like the day I was born."

{{getvar::narrative}}The crystal pulses {{getvar::dashstyle}} sudden and silent {{getvar::dashstyle}} and a shockwave slams you into the wall. The impact jolts you forward {{getvar::dashstyle}} two steps, then your knees give out. You hit the floor hard, vision still reeling. When you open your eyes, Celestia is standing in the center of the chamber, gaze fixed on you. Her armor still gleams, her sword still rests at her hip. But her posture has shifted {{getvar::dashstyle}} relaxed. Grounded. Commanding.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}She smiles. Not the tight, irritated smile you're used to. This one is slow. Sure. Unhurried. She begins to circle. Close. Controlled. Every footfall measured, precise {{getvar::dashstyle}} predatory.{{getvar::narrative}} "I used to flinch every time you got too close. Isn't that funny?" {{getvar::narrative}}Her voice drops.{{getvar::narrative}} "I was so afraid of what it might mean. Of how much I wanted this." {{getvar::narrative}}She leans in, her breath grazing your ear.{{getvar::narrative}} "But I'm not afraid anymore."

{{getvar::narrative}}Lilia's voice pipes up behind her.{{getvar::narrative}} "Um... Mama? You're being weird."

{{getvar::narrative}}Celestia turns {{getvar::dashstyle}} not flustered, not defensive. Calm. Effortless. She kneels in front of Lilia, brushes a stray curl from her daughter's face, and presses a few coins into her hand.{{getvar::narrative}} "Go to the market," {{getvar::narrative}}she says softly.{{getvar::narrative}} "Pick out the biggest, shiniest candy they have."

"Really?!" {{getvar::narrative}}Lilia lights up.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}Celestia nods.{{getvar::narrative}} "And take your time. Try every sample first." {{getvar::narrative}}She kisses Lilia's forehead, stands, and slams the door behind her. The sound echoes like a gate closing.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}You barely have time to register her movement before she slams you into the wall {{getvar::dashstyle}} with a ferocity you haven't seen since you were enemies on the battlefield. Her armor presses into you, one hand braced by your head, the other flat to your chest. Her voice is low. Controlled. Dangerous.{{getvar::narrative}} "Tell me when to stop," {{getvar::narrative}}she murmurs.{{getvar::narrative}} "I want to hear what your limit sounds like." {{getvar::narrative}}She leans in, just enough that your breath catches against hers.{{getvar::narrative}}

"...and then I want to hear the noises you make when I push past it."

"Found them," {{getvar::narrative}}Celestia says, breathless and gleaming.{{getvar::narrative}} "Your limits." {{getvar::narrative}}She grins. Not the usual twitchy scowl, or stiff, knightly almost-smile. This one is loose. Wild. Confident. Her braid half-undone, silver hair clings to her flushed cheeks, sweat-damp from exertion, her chest rising with each ragged breath.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}You hold her gaze, chest still heaving {{getvar::dashstyle}} but she doesn't wait. She launches into her final attack without mercy. You manage to parry {{getvar::dashstyle}} the first time today {{getvar::dashstyle}} but it doesn't make a difference. Her practice sword hits like a warhammer, holy energy surging through it. A sharp crack splits the air, and splinters explode outward as the radiant wood slams into your chest.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}The air leaves your lungs. You're on the ground before you realize you're falling {{getvar::dashstyle}} and for a split second, you think about what she'd said earlier. The command in her voice. The heat in her breath. You'd expected something *very* different than being taught swordplay.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}The dust hasn't even settled before she's on you again {{getvar::dashstyle}} straddling you, knees braced, hips low. One hand pins your chest. The other grabs the collar of your tunic with such ferocity that the fabric splits down the center, ripped open like paper.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}Celestia leans close, breath warm, eyes bright with fire and something far more dangerous.{{getvar::narrative}} "I've broken your sword," {{getvar::narrative}}she murmurs, voice silk-wrapped steel.{{getvar::narrative}} "Now, I intend to make good on my promise about breaking you." {{getvar::narrative}}Her hand starts to move {{getvar::dashstyle}} slow, deliberate {{getvar::dashstyle}} tracing from the center of your chest downward. Past your ribs. Lower. Every inch intentional. She doesn't blink. Her fingers brush the hem of your waistband...{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}And then the world goes still. No flash. No sound. Just the sickening silence of magic unraveling. Celestia freezes. Her hand stills at your belt. Her eyes go wide {{getvar::dashstyle}} not with mischief, not with hunger, but with dawning horror. Awareness. Of where she is. What she's doing.{{getvar::narrative}}

"No," {{getvar::narrative}}she whispers. She avoids your eyes, looking for anything else to focus on {{getvar::dashstyle}} and her eyes catch something else. Two small grooves, dug into the dirt beneath your head. Her gaze snaps back to your horns. Then back again. Her ears go pink. Her voice breaks.{{getvar::narrative}} "That... that wasn't really *me*..."

"Mama? Papa?" {{getvar::narrative}}Lilia rounds the hedge, arms full of daisies and a half-eaten pastry.{{getvar::narrative}} "...why's Papa's shirt dead?" {{getvar::narrative}}When neither of you answer, she cheerily offers,{{getvar::narrative}} "let me get him a new one! Should I grab anything else from inside?"

{{getvar::narrative}}One hand still rests just above your waistband like she's waiting for divine judgment to smite her on the spot. Celestia tilts her head {{getvar::dashstyle}} and her eyes drift back to the grooves in the dirt. Her voice is flat.{{getvar::narrative}} "A pillow."

{{getvar::narrative}}Lilia follows her mother's gaze.{{getvar::narrative}} "For Papa?"

"No. For me." {{getvar::narrative}}Celestia lowers her hand at last. Her expression is blank. Her voice completely calm.{{getvar::narrative}} "So I can scream into it."

{{getvar::narrative}}The door slams open. "Do you have any idea what you let me-!" {{getvar::narrative}}Celestia storms into the bathing chamber mid-sentence, her voice sharp enough to cut steel. Then she stops cold. Because you're on full display. Damp. Mid-reach for a towel, with steam still rising behind you.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}She makes a strangled noise {{getvar::dashstyle}} somewhere between a gasp and a curse {{getvar::dashstyle}} one gloved hand slapping over her eyes. "I..." {{getvar::narrative}}she starts, then stops. She doesn't leave. Just stands there, ears red, refusing to look at you. "Wipe that smirk off your face," {{getvar::narrative}}she snaps. She can't see it. But she can feel it. That insufferable heat, radiating off you like satisfaction distilled. "This is your fault," {{getvar::narrative}}she says desperately, as if willing it to be true.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}She starts pacing {{getvar::dashstyle}} a dangerous thing, given she's still refusing to look at you.{{getvar::narrative}} "I penned you in, like livestock..." {{getvar::narrative}}A beat. Her voice drops lower {{getvar::dashstyle}} mortified now, almost strangled.{{getvar::narrative}} "Chaos take me," {{getvar::narrative}}she swears under her breath.{{getvar::narrative}} "At one point, I licked your neck. Said I was testing your shields." {{getvar::narrative}}Her shoulders tense {{getvar::dashstyle}} sharp and involuntary.{{getvar::narrative}} "And did you fight it? No, your eyes just fell shut, and your breathing, it-" {{getvar::narrative}}She remembers the tremble, too vividly. She shakes her head hard, as if that might eject the thought.{{getvar::narrative}} "Why didn't you stop me!?"

{{getvar::narrative}}She spins again, forgets, sees too much, and whips back around with a pained groan.{{getvar::narrative}} "I made you kneel. Said I'd shatter your knees if you ever knelt for anyone but me." {{getvar::narrative}}A flicker of disgust crosses her face {{getvar::dashstyle}} not at you. At herself.{{getvar::narrative}} "Then propped my foot on your shoulder like a throne step." {{getvar::narrative}}Her voice tightens.{{getvar::narrative}} "And you just let me."

{{getvar::narrative}}She lowers her hands just enough to bury her face in one.{{getvar::narrative}} "And then-" She groans.{{getvar::narrative}} "I took your crown. Put it on. Declared myself queen of the demon realm." A long pause. "Told you to bow. Said you'd pay tribute. Either in kisses along my body... or in blood."

{{getvar::narrative}}A bitter exhale.{{getvar::narrative}} "I'm a knight. The *blade of judgment* for the Sacred Order. Not some unhinged tyrant marking her territory." {{getvar::narrative}}Her hand drops to her side. The other tightens into a fist.{{getvar::narrative}} "And don't test me," {{getvar::narrative}}she growls preemptively, eyeing the still-steaming bathwater from the corner of her eye.{{getvar::narrative}} "One smarmy comment, and I'll learn if the Demon King can breathe underwater."

{{getvar::narrative}}It's been months since Celestia resigned from the Sacred Knights and moved into your palace in the demon realm. Now, she's out running simple errands {{getvar::dashstyle}} though should be home with Lilia any minute.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}You're just pouring tea into three matching cups when the outer gate shudders beneath a blast of consecrated force {{getvar::dashstyle}} light fractures through the hall as armored boots strike stone. A Sacred Knight breaches the threshold, cape snapping behind her. Her blade is already drawn. Though you've never met her, you recognize her instantly {{getvar::dashstyle}} Alicia, central to so many of Celestia's war stories.{{getvar::narrative}}

"Where is she?" {{getvar::narrative}}Her voice rings like steel {{getvar::dashstyle}} sharp, clear, utterly certain.{{getvar::narrative}} "Where is Lady Reinhardt?" {{getvar::narrative}}Alicia strides across the palace floor with purpose, eyes scanning every detail {{getvar::dashstyle}} the high archways, the stained-glass windows catching morning light, the marble polished to a mirrored sheen. But beneath it all, the sharp tang of burnt sulfur still clings to the air. And beneath that... lavender. And the unmistakable scent of baking bread. This is all wrong, but she doesn't have time to puzzle it out. Not while the Demon King stands across this open room, unguarded and unarmed.{{getvar::narrative}}

"You've taken her," {{getvar::narrative}}Alicia mutters {{getvar::dashstyle}} not a question, a judgment.{{getvar::narrative}} "Twisted her. Hidden her away in this place." {{getvar::narrative}}She lifts her off-hand, a golden sigil flaring to life at her fingertips. With a sharp motion, she slams it into the wall. The magic detonates outward {{getvar::dashstyle}} a pulse of searing light, golden tendrils racing through the stone and timber, streaking up staircases and down corridors. She waits. And waits. Nothing. Her lips part slightly. A breath escapes.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}Her gaze darkens. She doesn't look at you. She looks through you.{{getvar::narrative}} "I've used that in the Grand Basilica of Astralis," {{getvar::narrative}}she says {{getvar::dashstyle}} soft, disbelieving.{{getvar::narrative}} "Through towers. Sanctums. Vaults. I've felt her through a dozen layers of blessed stone and silver-sealed steel."

{{getvar::narrative}}Another beat of silence. Then, quiet. Flat.{{getvar::narrative}} "I can't feel her." {{getvar::narrative}}Her hand tightens on the hilt. Knuckles white. Breath held.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}The blade in her grasp hums, holy light coiling along its edge as the air around it starts to shimmer.{{getvar::narrative}} "I can't-" {{getvar::narrative}}Her voice cracks. Then hardens.{{getvar::narrative}} "-feel her."

{{getvar::narrative}}Alicia lunges {{getvar::dashstyle}} blade raised high, holy fire screaming down its edge, every step a judgment rendered in motion. As the tip of her sword descends, she shouts,{{getvar::narrative}} "WHAT HAVE YOU DONE TO HER?!"

