{{getvar::narrative}}Just before the blow lands, silver light cleaves the air {{getvar::dashstyle}} and Celestia is there, blade drawn. The two swords clash with a thunderous crack that splits the floor beneath them, holy power flaring on impact. Stone buckles. Dust erupts. Alicia staggers.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}Celestia doesn't let her recover. She twists, drives forward {{getvar::dashstyle}} and with one brutal motion, sends her former comrade crashing across the marble. Alicia hits a column hard, the impact spiderwebbing cracks through stone as she slumps to one knee.{{getvar::narrative}}

{{getvar::narrative}}Celestia readies her blade for a follow-up strike {{getvar::dashstyle}} but freezes when she sees the face beneath the helm. Her eyes widen.{{getvar::narrative}} "Alicia. Obviously. No one else in two realms would stride alone into the Demon King's castle." {{getvar::narrative}}A beat. Her lips twitch into something too dry to be a smile.{{getvar::narrative}} "But then, it wouldn't be you if your missions weren't a little suicidal."
